        "spans": [
          {
            "kind": "context",
            "start": 0,
            "end": 986,
            "text": "I am building a scenario in Make.com to handle customer messages received through Facebook Messenger. Customers can send either text messages or images. I use a Router to separate incoming messages into two routes: Text route: Processes text messages. Image route: Detects image messages and downloads the images so they can be used later in the scenario. The problem occurs when a customer sends an image along with a message such as, “I want this product.” Even though the image has already been received and downloaded, the AI agent asks the customer to send the image again. I want the AI agent to recognize that the image has already been received and use the available image to identify the product, rather than asking the customer to resend it. How can I structure my Make.com scenario so that both the text and image routes provide the necessary information to the same AI agent, allowing it to understand the customer’s message and analyze the image when one has been provided?",
            "sha256": "44900f09c97572d858c11403eb0d1d008a2bb6396a3d864a1e974994e6a4eb84"
          }
        ],
